  "page1": "Safety                                                                          Reliability\nThe T25 / T30 benefits from a long tiller with a low mounting point            The highly durable, robot welded construction of the pallet truck\nensuring a large safety clearance between operator and chassis.               ensures consistent reliability and a long life in reference to de-\n Creep speed and proportional speed functions, available as options,            manding applications. Each heavy cast fork tip can support a load\n provide optimum safety during load transfer or when manoeuvring                of 2000 kg without deformation. The arrow shaped fork tips also\n in tight corners.                                                               facilitate easy entry into every type of pallet and due to shrink\n Performance                                                                      wrapping, it ensures also fast, efficient, and safe load handling.\n This pallet truck is ideal for e\n                                 fficient handling of heavier loads.              Service\n The compact and powerful 1.5 kW AC drive unit and the innovative                  A maintenance-free AC motor reduces service costs. Operating\n castor wheels ensure the optimum mix of stability and traction in                 parameters can be individually adjusted to the operator‘s needs via\n all situations. This all adds up to e  fficient and safe transfer of loads        the CAN-bus system. The service engineer has fast, easy access\n up to 3000 kg.                                                                     not only to truck data, via the CAN-bus system, but also to all main\n Comfort                                                                       internal components.\n All controls on the ergonomic tiller head can be easily operated by\n either hand. A Creep speed button offers utmost maneuverabil-\n ity in confined areas. Generous storage compartments for work\n equipment such as shrink wrap eases the operator’s tasks.",
  "other": "ACCORDING TO VDI 2198",
